---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, LEGAL } from '../../lib/site.js';

// Where Web3Forms sends a contractor after a successful submission — see the
// hidden `redirect` field on /get-listed/. Without this page that redirect
// would land on a 404, and without the redirect the contractor would land on
// api.web3forms.com's own generic success page, off this site entirely.
//
// noindex: it has no value in search, it only makes sense as the second half
// of a submission, and an indexed thank-you page is a classic way to get a
// thin, orphaned URL into the index. noindex also drops it from the sitemap.
//
// No <form> and nothing that can be resubmitted: a reload of this URL is inert.
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Listing Request Received"
  description="Your garage door listing request has been received. What happens next, and how long it usually takes."
  canonical="/get-listed/thanks/"
  noindex={true}
>
  <div class="wrap-narrow">
    <span class="eyebrow">Get listed</span>
    <h1 style="margin:.5rem 0 .75rem;">Thanks — we have your details</h1>

    <div class="answer-box">
      <p>
        Your listing request has reached us. We read every one, and we will either add the
        listing or reply telling you why not. Both outcomes get an answer.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-4" style="font-size:1.2rem;">What happens next</h2>
    <p style="max-width:62ch;">
      We check the details against the business data we already hold, and where you have
      given a state licence number we check it against the state register. {SITE.name}
      {' '}covers California, Florida and Arizona for licence checks, because those are the
      only three states that license garage door work as its own trade.
    </p>
    <p style="max-width:62ch;" class="mt-2">
      A city page needs at least three listings before it publishes. If yours is the first
      in your city it is not lost — it is held and publishes automatically once the city
      reaches that threshold.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-4" style="font-size:1.2rem;">If you need to change something</h2>
    <p style="max-width:62ch;">
      Email <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.contactEmail}`}>{LEGAL.contactEmail}</a> with the
      business name and what needs correcting. That is also the address to use to have a
      listing removed — we do not require a reason.
    </p>

    <p class="claim-note mt-3">
      While you are here: <a href="/guides/hiring-a-garage-door-company/">what homeowners
      are told to ask you</a> before they book. It is the same page your prospective
      customers read, and it is worth knowing what is on it.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
